@danishprakash @mheon

> adding an e2e test for this is straightforward and doesn't require a refactor. You could also potentially extend the existing "teardown with secret" e2e test with a failure case.

Yes. `teardown prints a secret removal error` extends that test. It plays the secret, replaces `secretsdata.json` with a directory, and runs `kube down`. The command exits 0 and stderr contains `deleting secret newsecret`.
